; Timing annotations for usb_enum.pasm at FULL speed (48 MHz, TURN = 4), kept
; beside the source so the firmware file stays untouched (docs/timing-check.md):
;   python -m pe.timing firmware/usb_enum.pasm --timing firmware/usb_enum.timing -D DP=0 -D DM=1 -D TURN=4
; Same conventions as usb_fs_dev.pasm: the core sees the host's J 2..6 ticks after
; the frame end reaches the firmware (tok_end and d_end are 2 ticks after the
; `in line` that returned T = 1); pads: adjust=3..4; the line transmitter is idle
; when a response starts (stall=...:0).
@point in_wait at=got_in              ; wait 1 pin DM
@point in_out at=got_in+2             ; out line, 16: SYNC + DATA0/DATA1/STALL
@point hs_wait at=handshake           ; wait 1 pin DM
@point hs_out at=handshake+2          ; out line, 16: SYNC + ACK/STALL
@point lost_ack at=tok_end+6          ; call commit: a token to the new address, status ACK lost
; in_ta excludes `lost_ack`: it assumes the first token to the new address after
; a lost status-stage ACK is a SETUP, as a host starts every control transfer.
; in_ta_any includes it, and FAILS: an IN there is answered up to 30 clocks
; after the host's EOP (measured on the model: 27.4-28.2), past 6.5 bit times.
@deadline in_ta from=in_wait.cond after=tok_end:2..6 to=in_out avoid=idle,got_setup,expect,lost_ack stall=in_out:0 min=8 max=26 adjust=3..4 reach=conditional "IN token -> DATA/STALL (r1 prepared ahead)"
@deadline in_ta_any from=in_wait.cond after=tok_end:2..6 to=in_out avoid=idle,got_setup,expect stall=in_out:0 min=8 max=26 adjust=3..4 "the same, with the lost-ACK commit path"
@deadline data_ta from=hs_wait.cond after=d_end:2..6 to=hs_out avoid=idle stall=hs_out:0 min=8 max=26 adjust=3..4 "DATA0/1 -> ACK/STALL"
@deadline rx_bit from=d_bit to=d_bit.enter avoid=d_end max=4 reach=conditional "DATA receive loop: a bit every 4 clocks"
